        { "text": "$[0,\\infty)$", "why": "Treated $x^3$ like a square root, but a cube has no radicand restriction." },
        { "text": "$(-\\infty,0)\\cup(0,\\infty)$", "why": "Excluded $x=0$, but $x^3$ has no denominator to restrict it." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "There is no denominator and no square root, so nothing is excluded.\nDomain: all real $x$, or $(-\\infty,\\infty)$."
    },
    {
