      "options": [
        { "text": "$(-\\infty,\\frac{7}{2})$", "correct": true },
        { "text": "$(-\\infty,\\frac{7}{2}]$", "why": "Used $\\geq$ for a strict surd-in-denominator that must be $>0$." },
        { "text": "$(\\frac{7}{2},\\infty)$", "why": "Reversed the inequality when dividing by $-2$." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "The root is in the denominator, so the radicand must be strictly positive.\n$7-2x>0$\n$7>2x$\n$x<\\frac{7}{2}$\nDomain: $(-\\infty,\\frac{7}{2})$"
    },
    {
